## 3. ER diagramy

> **Pravidlo:** každá DB má vlastní ER diagram. Cross-DB FK se zmiňuje v textu, ne v diagramu (mermaid `erDiagram` to neumí čistě).

### 3.1 `[{{DB1}}]`

```mermaid
erDiagram
    SUBJECTS ||--o{ SUBJECTS_ADRESY : ma
    SUBJECTS ||--o{ SUBJECTS_NAZVY : ma
    SUBJECTS ||--o{ TASKS : "queue per subject"
    SUBJECTS {
        int id_subject PK
        nvarchar ic UK
        nvarchar dic
        datetime last_check
    }
    SUBJECTS_ADRESY {
        int id_adresa PK
        int id_subject FK
        nvarchar ulice
        datetime datum_od
        datetime datum_do "NULL = aktivní"
    }
    SUBJECTS_NAZVY {
        int id_nazev PK
        int id_subject FK
        nvarchar nazev
        datetime datum_od
        datetime datum_do
    }
    TASKS {
        int id_task PK
        nvarchar ic
        int state
        datetime created_at
    }
```

### 3.2 `[{{DB2}}]`

```mermaid
erDiagram
    DOCUMENTS {
        int id_document PK
        int id_subject_appdb "FK do {{DB1}}.subjects (bez DB constraint)"
        varbinary hash_payload UK
        varbinary payload_zip
        int status
        datetime inserted
    }
```

**Cross-DB poznámka:** `[{{DB2}}].[dbo].[Documents].id_subject_appdb` referencuje `[{{DB1}}].[dbo].[subjects].id_subject` — bez FK constraint, integrita zajištěna v aplikaci.

## 4. Parametry SP (detail)

### `{{sp_CreateSubject}}`

| Parametr | Typ | Direction | Význam |
|---|---|---|---|
| `@ic` | `NVARCHAR(20)` | IN | IČ subjektu |
| `@id_subject` | `INT` | OUT | Vrácený nový PK |

**SQL:**
```sql
CREATE PROCEDURE {{sp_CreateSubject}}
    @ic NVARCHAR(20),
    @id_subject INT OUTPUT
AS
BEGIN
    INSERT INTO subjects (ic, vlozeno) VALUES (@ic, GETDATE());
    SET @id_subject = SCOPE_IDENTITY();
END
```

